MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Harvest Moon feels like a natural next choice because its warm, rootsy songwriting connects with what draws me to Old Sock and You Should Be So Lucky.",
    "Days of Future Passed fits the classic rock side of my listening, even though Harvest Moon is closer to what I want right now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "CHRISTMAS 25TH ANNIVERSARY misses my current interest because I am not looking for seasonal music, and Disco Inferno does not fit the blues and roots rock mood I want.",
    "Titles such as Fun, Bad Attitude, and No Regrets leave me unsure which release I would be choosing. Without a recognizable connection to my listening, I would pass."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices feel too broadly connected to music in general; I need a closer connection to the sound and songwriting I have been choosing.",
    "An older or familiar-sounding title alone is not enough to interest me; Days of Future Passed appeals because I recognize its musical connection, not simply because it is an older release."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The blues and roots rock thread across my recent listening matters more to me than a loose connection between album titles.",
    "I rarely choose something just to explore, so a clear musical connection matters. Harvest Moon gives me that reason to listen now."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognize my classic rock interests but only a few connect clearly with the warm, rootsy music I want right now."
}
